  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Stablecoin market cap fell 6.2% over 30D:</strong> Stablecoin market cap at $273.87B (6.2% lower over 30D). Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/moonpay-seeks-us-bank-charter-for-stablecoin-custody-services?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MoonPay seeks US bank charter for stablecoin, custody services</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Stablecoin market structure remains concentration-led:</strong> leadership is still defined by a small set of large issuers/platforms; share shifts matter as much as aggregate market-cap growth. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/11/19/sky-s-usds-stablecoin-shrinks-35-as-usd1-5-billion-exits-reserves-after-illicit-finance-report\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sky&#x27;s USDS stablecoin shrinks 35% as $1.5 billion exits reserves after illicit-finance report</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Policy and reserves are resetting issuer priorities:</strong> Issuer and platform share can shift before aggregate market cap does, because policy and reserve quality determine which names institutions will hold. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/11/19/trump-s-democratic-sec-pick-suggests-tokenization-policy-deserves-full-rule-process\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Trump&#x27;s Democratic SEC pick suggests tokenization policy deserves full rule process</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations